<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75759" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδᾰμ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲ
			ἀμός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not any
				one, no one</i>, 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδείς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				57.2
			</span></i>: used only in pl. and only by 
				Ion.
			 writers ( =
			
				Att.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδένες</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
				οὐδαμοί, οὐδαμῶν</span>, etc., <i>none</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.18
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				24
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				57
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρήγματα . . οὐδαμῶν
				Ἑλληνικῶν τῶν οὐ πολλὸν μέζω</span>, i.e. much greater
			than any Greek power, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.145
			</span></i>: rarely in fem., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδαμὰς ἄλλας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.114
				</span></i>
			.—Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδαμός</span>.</div>
